Here's an example C++ program that reads a text file line by line and counts the number of occurrences of a specific word in the file:

```
#include <iostream>
#include <fstream>
#include <string>

using namespace std;

int main() {
    string wordToCount;
    int count = 0;

    // Prompt user for word to count
    cout << "Enter the word to count: ";
    cin >> wordToCount;

    // Open file for reading
    ifstream inputFile("input.txt");

    // Read file line by line
    string line;
    while (getline(inputFile, line)) {
        // Count occurrences of word in line
        size_t pos = 0;
        while ((pos = line.find(wordToCount, pos)) != string::npos) {
            count++;
            pos += wordToCount.length();
        }
    }

    // Close file
    inputFile.close();

    // Display count
    cout << "The word \"" << wordToCount << "\" appears " << count << " times in the file." << endl;

    return 0;
}
```

In this program, we first prompt the user to enter the word they want to count. We then open the input file for reading and read it line by line. For each line, we count the number of occurrences of the specified word using the `find()` method of the `string` class. We keep track of the count in the `count` variable. Finally, we display the count to the user.
